{
	"name": "Derring Do",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/skills/movement/ball-spinning-blue.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 16th level, your scoundrel gains the ability to engage in a bit more derring do than normal, bounding or swinging or sneaking into position. When they move into position to flank a creature, they may roll an Acrobatics, Athletics, or Stealth check against the creature’s combat maneuver DC as a bonus action. On a successful roll, the scoundrel’s backstab dice become d8s until the start of the creature’s next turn.</p><p>Once your scoundrel has successfully used this ability they cannot do so again until they have taken a long rest.</p>",
